{"id": "context-2-code-2", "kind": "code", "arm": "performance", "image": "sha256:47c9d5fc5eb28fd12ef6219fbbfe7cf3863e00aa0535da377cadfc9a181bcd41", "context_sha256": "dddbb392b2d87b17c973d3d33f28a66edaecc943f29fe0d5dc55116f22c041ec", "prompt_sha256": "a7c20753a42bb613c653845f13aa731b9bcf56aea8ccbdb6df9dae8b2013e306", "output_sha256": "c5d3e9f452a7097cfb1d118a86efec818c3615baaa1a55a95064d7299b6ee67c", "output": "```python\ndef solve(lines, metric):\n    total = 0.0\n    for line in lines:\n        line = line.strip()\n        if not line or line.startswith(\"#\"):\n            continue\n        # Find the last space that separates the metric name from the value\n        # The metric name may be followed by '{' for labels\n        # We need to extract the metric name part before any '{' or space\n        # Format: metric_name{labels} value  OR  metric_name value\n        \n        # Find the position of the last space\n        last_space = line.rfind(' ')\n        if last_space == -1:\n            continue\n            \n        name_part = line[:last_space]\n        value_part = line[last_space + 1:]\n        \n        # Check if name_part ends with '}' (labeled metric)\n        if name_part.endswith('}'):\n            # Find the opening brace\n            brace_start = name_part.find('{')\n            if brace_start == -1:\n                continue\n            name = name_part[:brace_start]\n        else:\n            name = name_part\n            \n        if name == metric:\n            try:\n                total += float(value_part)\n            except ValueError:\n                pass\n                \n    return total\n```", "score": {"passed": true, "test_results": [{"passed": true, "actual": 4.0}, {"passed": true, "actual": 0.0}, {"passed": true, "actual": 97.5}]}, "ttft_s": 1.7771231690003333, "wall_s": 5.616978191001181, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 32761, "total_tokens": 33031, "completion_tokens": 270, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0